For a Node.js `http.request()` using a Unix domain socket, pass `socketPath` and omit `host`/`port`:

```js
import { request } from 'node:http';

const req = request(
  {
    socketPath: '/tmp/example-node.sock',
    path: '/',
  },
  (res) => {
    res.on('data', (chunk) => console.log(String(chunk)));
  },
);

req.end();
```

`socketPath` cannot be used together with `host` or `port`. Built-in proxy settings (`proxyEnv`, `HTTP_PROXY`, etc.) are ignored when the request is made to a Unix domain socket.
